    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23-a4">

                <pb facs="0125" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg55"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations of Nicaragua</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1883-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 3, 1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm to you my
                    telegram of the 28th of the last month, which is as follows: [See above.]</p>
                <p>At the same time, I inclose in this note a certified copy of the communication
                    which, on the 26th of the same, the minister of Costa Rica addressed to this
                    department, <pb facs="0126" n="56" xml:id="pg56"/> making the declaration
                    referred to in the preinserted telegram. Notwithstanding that up to the present
                    time no answer has been received from Honduras and Salvador, in view, of that
                    which your excellency was pleased to give by telegraph the 30th of the said
                    month, the Government of Nicaragua has resolved to suspend for the present the
                    sending of its delegates to the projected diet.</p>
                <p>I reiterate, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. J. MEDINA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">His Excellency the Minister of
                            Foreign Relations</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">of the Republic of
                            Guatemala.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
